WEBVTT

00:07.173 --> 00:08.925
The game will now commence.

00:17.350 --> 00:18.351
"The game"?

00:21.896 --> 00:23.064
What game?

00:24.983 --> 00:28.361
What "game" do they mean?

00:30.613 --> 00:33.908
Where… did everyone go?

00:34.409 --> 00:36.870
Shinagawa Station was empty too.

00:39.456 --> 00:40.832
Shit.

00:42.625 --> 00:43.877
I'm trippin' hard.

00:50.050 --> 00:51.968
The game is Fortunes.

00:56.389 --> 01:00.685
Test your luck by drawing ten fortunes.

01:00.769 --> 01:02.312
FORTUNES

01:02.896 --> 01:09.903
To win, decipher the meaning
of the fortunes and survive to the end.

01:10.653 --> 01:14.032
However, only one draw
is allowed per person.

01:14.532 --> 01:18.745
There is a one-minute time limit per draw.

01:20.622 --> 01:23.124
Game start.

01:24.918 --> 01:27.587
Is there some sort of festival today?

01:29.547 --> 01:33.927
The announcement mentioned
"survive to the end."

01:34.010 --> 01:35.386
Does that mean

01:35.970 --> 01:37.680
we die if we're wrong?

01:38.348 --> 01:39.849
No way.

01:40.350 --> 01:42.185
Sounds fun to me.

01:52.904 --> 01:55.740
He's on drugs.

01:57.742 --> 01:58.701
Here goes!

02:08.211 --> 02:09.963
Seventeen.

02:12.298 --> 02:13.675
Let's see…

02:15.093 --> 02:16.678
Seventeen!

02:20.682 --> 02:22.767
First draw. Begin.

02:31.693 --> 02:33.069
"Great luck."

02:34.362 --> 02:36.823
"Everything you do will go well."

02:36.906 --> 02:39.242
- Check it out!
- Nice one!

02:39.325 --> 02:40.368
Right?

02:40.451 --> 02:42.912
We don't know whether that's good yet.

02:50.378 --> 02:54.007
Maybe nothing happens with "great luck."

02:56.009 --> 02:58.636
Okay, then let's keep drawing.

02:58.720 --> 02:59.721
What?

03:00.555 --> 03:01.764
We're doing this?

03:01.848 --> 03:03.808
I wanna try.

03:04.475 --> 03:05.435
Go ahead.

03:16.446 --> 03:17.572
Twenty-one.

03:20.200 --> 03:22.202
Second draw. Begin.

03:25.955 --> 03:26.873
"Good luck."

03:27.373 --> 03:30.251
"Wishes gradually come true.
Marriage prospects are good."

03:30.335 --> 03:33.796
"Study hard with peace of mind.
West is unlucky."

03:37.675 --> 03:39.052
There's a math problem.

03:40.136 --> 03:41.471
May we see?

03:46.935 --> 03:48.811
Should we solve it?

03:50.230 --> 03:52.023
- Your answer, please.
- Fifteen.

03:52.523 --> 03:54.567
- Fifteen?
- Fifteen.

03:54.651 --> 03:55.735
Isn't it 18?

03:56.444 --> 03:57.946
- It's five.
- Fourteen!

03:58.029 --> 04:00.240
- Which one?
- Come on. There's no time!

04:00.323 --> 04:01.491
Ten more seconds.

04:02.367 --> 04:04.160
The answer is 18!

04:04.244 --> 04:06.204
- I said 15.
- That's totally wrong.

04:06.829 --> 04:08.706
The answer is 15.

04:09.207 --> 04:10.041
Told you.

04:10.541 --> 04:11.751
- See?
- Sorry.

04:12.252 --> 04:14.254
If you answer incorrectly,

04:14.337 --> 04:17.632
the difference will determine
the number of flaming arrows.

04:17.715 --> 04:19.968
Please be careful.

04:20.802 --> 04:21.719
Flaming arrows?

04:33.439 --> 04:34.857
What the hell?

06:03.404 --> 06:04.906
Please.

06:11.496 --> 06:12.789
Forty-five.

06:13.456 --> 06:14.999
Forty-five…

06:19.420 --> 06:21.547
Third draw. Begin.

06:22.173 --> 06:23.299
"Moderate luck."

06:24.258 --> 06:25.259
And the problem?

06:27.762 --> 06:31.599
"How many people does it take
for there to be at least a 50% chance

06:31.682 --> 06:33.768
that two share the same birthday?"

06:34.268 --> 06:36.062
"One, 23."

06:36.145 --> 06:37.855
"Two, 78."

06:37.939 --> 06:39.857
"Three, 183."

06:39.941 --> 06:42.151
"Four, 365."

06:42.235 --> 06:43.986
I've got no idea.

06:44.070 --> 06:45.696
It's a probability problem.

06:45.780 --> 06:47.782
It's probably more than 100.

06:47.865 --> 06:49.659
It's probably 183, right?

06:49.742 --> 06:51.494
I think it's 23.

06:51.577 --> 06:52.995
Yeah, 23.

06:53.079 --> 06:54.622
Maybe it's 183?

06:55.748 --> 06:56.958
Twenty seconds left.

06:57.041 --> 06:57.875
Okay.

06:59.836 --> 07:00.878
The answer is

07:02.046 --> 07:03.506
number two, 78.

07:03.589 --> 07:05.091
What? Why?

07:05.174 --> 07:06.676
I took the middle ground!

07:07.176 --> 07:10.763
- Please!
- The answer is number one, 23 people.

07:10.847 --> 07:12.557
- See?
- Difference, 55.

07:25.862 --> 07:27.530
I'm sorry!

07:28.698 --> 07:30.741
Fourth draw. Begin.

07:30.825 --> 07:34.203
"How long does it take
for blood pumped from the heart

07:34.704 --> 07:38.166
to make one round trip
through the entire body?"

07:39.041 --> 07:40.751
"One, five seconds."

07:41.335 --> 07:42.837
"Two, 30 seconds."

07:43.421 --> 07:45.256
"Three, 80 seconds."

07:46.340 --> 07:48.009
Number three, 80 seconds!

07:49.218 --> 07:52.054
The answer is number two, 30 seconds.

07:52.138 --> 07:53.764
Difference, 50.

08:03.733 --> 08:09.322
"Fifty zoo animals
flipped over sequentially."

08:09.405 --> 08:12.033
"What was the lion's number
in the sequence?"

08:13.326 --> 08:14.410
Is that it?

08:14.494 --> 08:15.536
A riddle?

08:16.621 --> 08:17.747
Forty-seventh!

08:19.165 --> 08:21.667
The answer is 17th.

08:21.751 --> 08:22.627
Why?

08:22.710 --> 08:27.465
"Lion" flipped upside down is "No. 17."

08:27.548 --> 08:28.466
What the hell?

08:28.549 --> 08:30.134
Difference, 30.

08:35.264 --> 08:39.519
"The Roman numeral I is one,
V is five, and X is ten."

08:39.602 --> 08:41.979
"What does L equal?"

08:43.272 --> 08:44.232
One hundred!

08:44.982 --> 08:47.068
The answer is 50.

08:47.151 --> 08:48.027
Sorry!

08:48.110 --> 08:49.320
Difference, 50.

08:53.824 --> 08:55.618
Difference, 55.

09:11.300 --> 09:13.469
Eighth draw. Begin.

09:46.502 --> 09:47.795
Now I remember.

09:48.754 --> 09:50.923
- Arisu, live on for us.
- Karube!

09:54.969 --> 09:56.012
That's right.

09:58.472 --> 10:01.058
I won a bunch of games here.

10:07.773 --> 10:08.774
All right!

10:08.858 --> 10:11.193
I'm gonna draw "great luck"!

10:11.277 --> 10:12.612
You can do it!

10:19.952 --> 10:22.288
Ninth draw. Begin.

10:22.371 --> 10:23.789
"Minor luck."

10:24.290 --> 10:26.542
I'm toast if it's a thinking problem.

10:26.626 --> 10:29.211
At least it's not "bad luck."
What's the problem?

10:29.295 --> 10:30.129
Let's see…

10:32.048 --> 10:36.677
"Milk is made from nutrients
in a cow's blood."

10:37.178 --> 10:41.682
"How many liters of blood
are needed to make one liter of milk?"

10:43.059 --> 10:43.893
Huh?

10:44.477 --> 10:45.645
Anyone know?

10:45.728 --> 10:47.813
Who the hell would know that?

10:48.397 --> 10:49.231
I don't know.

10:49.315 --> 10:50.650
- Twenty seconds left.
- Answer!

10:50.733 --> 10:53.235
Don't rush her. It makes it hard to think.

10:53.319 --> 10:54.695
There's no time! Hurry!

10:54.779 --> 10:56.572
I don't know stuff like this!

10:56.656 --> 10:57.907
Guess a number!

11:01.160 --> 11:02.662
Ten seconds left.

11:04.413 --> 11:05.539
The answer is…

11:07.708 --> 11:08.834
two liters.

11:10.503 --> 11:13.214
The answer is 450 liters.

11:13.297 --> 11:15.049
450 liters?

11:15.132 --> 11:16.717
That much?

11:16.801 --> 11:18.427
It's one liter of milk!

11:18.511 --> 11:21.389
- I'm sorry!
- Difference, 448.

11:23.432 --> 11:24.767
No way!

11:48.582 --> 11:49.583
I'm sorry!

11:50.209 --> 11:52.044
Never mind! Help me with this!

11:52.878 --> 11:53.754
Shit!

11:56.340 --> 11:58.843
It's too freakin' hot!

11:59.510 --> 12:00.344
Now then…

12:02.263 --> 12:03.389
This is gonna hurt.

12:07.852 --> 12:08.978
Sorry about this.

12:15.651 --> 12:16.944
- Huh?
- You okay?

12:18.279 --> 12:19.363
Don't pass out!

12:20.614 --> 12:21.532
All right.

12:23.492 --> 12:25.244
You know first aid?

12:25.327 --> 12:28.330
Only 'cause I can't see a doctor
without getting arrested.

12:28.414 --> 12:31.375
That should do it. You okay?

12:43.471 --> 12:45.806
- I'm burning up!
- The tenth draw's next.

12:46.682 --> 12:48.017
The last one, right?

12:48.726 --> 12:50.186
We'll win if you draw.

12:51.812 --> 12:52.813
Please.

12:53.814 --> 12:54.648
Got it.

12:56.233 --> 12:58.944
I can't take it anymore!

13:03.199 --> 13:05.284
Tenth draw. Begin.

13:12.041 --> 13:15.336
NUMBER 58
EXTREME BAD LUCK

13:15.419 --> 13:17.963
Look at you.

13:19.673 --> 13:21.091
Well done.

13:21.759 --> 13:23.594
- Sorry.
- What's the problem?

13:27.681 --> 13:30.476
"What is the world population
in billions?"

13:31.227 --> 13:32.061
Huh?

13:33.521 --> 13:37.775
I heard the world's population
increases by 80 million each year.

13:37.858 --> 13:40.194
It was about 7.88 billion a few years ago.

13:40.778 --> 13:43.906
A wrong answer means
hundreds of millions of arrows.

13:43.989 --> 13:45.616
No way that's possible.

13:46.534 --> 13:47.868
Twenty seconds left.

13:55.876 --> 13:57.211
Ten seconds left.

13:59.380 --> 14:00.840
7.9 billion.

14:02.967 --> 14:05.469
The answer is eight billion.

14:06.262 --> 14:08.305
- Seriously?
- Off by 100 million.

14:08.389 --> 14:12.101
That's impossible!
Where would that many arrows even…

14:24.238 --> 14:25.281
No way.

14:26.198 --> 14:29.118
A hundred million arrows.

14:29.201 --> 14:30.828
What are we gonna do?

14:30.911 --> 14:32.621
What do we do?

14:33.414 --> 14:35.749
Think.

14:37.918 --> 14:41.505
Decipher the meaning of the fortunes…

14:41.589 --> 14:44.842
"Study hard with peace of mind.
West is unlucky."

14:45.759 --> 14:47.386
DIRECTIONAL FORTUNE CHART

14:47.469 --> 14:48.429
WEST

14:51.181 --> 14:52.016
Direction.

14:52.099 --> 14:53.142
Huh?

14:53.225 --> 14:54.059
What?

14:54.143 --> 14:57.229
Could the fortune directions
tell us how to escape?

14:57.313 --> 14:59.815
- I threw mine away!
- What's your direction?

15:00.482 --> 15:01.984
"West is unlucky."

15:02.067 --> 15:03.944
The arrows came from that way.

15:04.028 --> 15:05.863
Anyone have a compass?

15:05.946 --> 15:08.782
- Who the hell would?
- Mine says northeast is unlucky.

15:08.866 --> 15:11.493
- Arrows came from that way!
- Mine says north is unlucky.

15:11.577 --> 15:12.870
Southeast is unlucky for me.

15:12.953 --> 15:14.622
- Mine says east.
- Mine is southwest.

15:14.705 --> 15:17.249
- Mine is south.
- It's blank on my fortune.

15:18.792 --> 15:20.502
What does "great luck" say?

15:22.296 --> 15:23.714
I said I threw it away!

15:23.797 --> 15:24.632
- Huh?
- What?!

15:24.715 --> 15:25.716
The arrows!

15:27.051 --> 15:28.093
Take cover!

15:29.720 --> 15:30.888
Northwest.

15:31.847 --> 15:34.808
- What?
- It's the only one missing.

15:34.892 --> 15:38.938
The "great luck" fortune was northwest.
That might be how we escape.

15:39.730 --> 15:42.149
- Come on! Hurry!
- Hurry!

15:53.285 --> 15:54.203
Stop.

15:55.162 --> 15:57.539
Now what? There's nothing here!

15:57.623 --> 15:59.249
There must be something.

15:59.333 --> 16:00.376
There's a well!

16:03.504 --> 16:04.922
It's full of dirt!

16:09.551 --> 16:12.471
The entrance had a long, steep stairway.

16:12.554 --> 16:13.555
So what?!

16:13.639 --> 16:14.640
That means

16:15.975 --> 16:17.393
within this compound,

16:19.019 --> 16:19.979
there must be…

16:25.901 --> 16:26.819
a tunnel!

16:32.908 --> 16:34.076
Here it comes.

16:37.788 --> 16:38.956
What the hell?

16:39.999 --> 16:43.293
How do we even survive that?

16:44.086 --> 16:45.796
- Some help here!
- Okay!

16:49.883 --> 16:51.343
It's too late.

17:09.611 --> 17:10.529
A tunnel.

17:13.741 --> 17:15.451
- Get in!
- Hurry!

17:30.716 --> 17:33.218
Come on! Hurry!

17:57.201 --> 17:58.035
This way.

18:07.753 --> 18:09.296
Game cleared.

18:12.341 --> 18:13.425
We made it.

18:47.084 --> 18:50.712
PROCEED 17 KM NORTHEAST
THE "GAME" STARTS AT SUNDOWN TOMORROW

18:50.796 --> 18:52.005
Another game?

18:54.842 --> 18:57.344
And if we refuse to go?

18:58.303 --> 19:01.306
Yeah, let's just not go.

19:01.390 --> 19:03.976
But if we don't go, then…

19:09.356 --> 19:11.066
There's no escaping the games.

20:37.110 --> 20:38.528
So this means…

20:41.823 --> 20:42.658
Yeah.

20:43.867 --> 20:46.453
We've been here before.

22:04.990 --> 22:06.033
Big Sister!

22:09.745 --> 22:10.579
"Big Sister"?

22:11.079 --> 22:12.664
Found something good.

22:13.206 --> 22:14.041
Here.

22:15.167 --> 22:17.085
- What's this?
- A cane.

22:17.169 --> 22:19.421
Thought it might help you walk.

22:19.504 --> 22:20.505
Thanks.

22:21.340 --> 22:22.549
It's so shiny.

22:22.632 --> 22:23.884
Yeah, glam gal style.

22:28.305 --> 22:30.891
Hey, Arisu. I found tons of stuff.

22:30.974 --> 22:32.267
Wow. That's great.

22:33.769 --> 22:35.729
- There's food too.
- Great.

22:39.232 --> 22:41.234
His eyes gave me chills.

22:42.944 --> 22:45.614
Like a creepy feeling he wasn't human.

22:48.033 --> 22:49.451
That man…

22:52.496 --> 22:53.830
I think I met him too.

22:55.582 --> 22:56.583
For real?

22:57.542 --> 22:58.919
About two years ago,

23:00.253 --> 23:03.590
I… went and did this.

23:04.383 --> 23:06.301
You poor thing.

23:08.011 --> 23:12.349
I was found unconscious, but I survived.

23:13.767 --> 23:14.726
But I was

23:16.353 --> 23:18.730
still broken from all the bullying.

23:20.607 --> 23:25.153
I continued being a recluse.
Nothing changed for me.

23:26.863 --> 23:27.864
And then…

23:29.157 --> 23:30.784
He gave you that card.

23:31.660 --> 23:32.494
Yeah.

23:33.286 --> 23:37.290
I think I met him before coming here too.

23:38.041 --> 23:39.042
Where?

23:40.919 --> 23:42.462
It's kind of embarrassing.

23:43.213 --> 23:45.549
I was invited to this healing circle…

23:46.049 --> 23:47.801
"Healing circle"?

23:49.302 --> 23:51.888
For housewives with family problems.

23:52.889 --> 23:54.599
Those kinds of groups exist.

23:55.684 --> 24:00.188
It was almost like he hypnotized me.

24:01.940 --> 24:04.651
So this guy is the Joker?

24:07.404 --> 24:12.742
We beat all the face cards
at their respective games,

24:14.327 --> 24:16.163
but we never battled the Joker.

24:17.456 --> 24:22.377
So does that mean
we're up against the Joker now?

24:23.211 --> 24:24.212
Most likely.

24:25.422 --> 24:28.967
The only thing I know is
we have something in common.

24:29.676 --> 24:32.637
We've all been here before.

24:33.305 --> 24:34.222
Right.

24:35.515 --> 24:37.851
I'm starting to remember.

24:39.144 --> 24:42.522
I once played games here too.

24:44.024 --> 24:47.777
I had a heart attack
while supervising club activities

24:48.737 --> 24:51.031
at the school I worked at.

24:51.907 --> 24:53.700
I was attacked by a stalker.

24:57.746 --> 24:59.956
For me, it was the Shibuya meteorite.

25:00.832 --> 25:01.833
But the games…

25:04.586 --> 25:06.254
I don't wanna remember them.

25:25.106 --> 25:27.984
Arisu, have you also been here before?

25:30.529 --> 25:31.404
Yeah.

26:01.810 --> 26:03.228
Unbelievable.

26:03.853 --> 26:07.148
He came here of his own free will
to get his wife back?

26:07.816 --> 26:09.234
You poor thing.

26:09.317 --> 26:11.736
- You've never known love, have you?
- Huh?

26:12.362 --> 26:15.740
A husband's duty is to cherish his wife.

26:16.241 --> 26:20.078
But what are the odds
of finding his wife here?

26:20.579 --> 26:23.623
Well, I'd say about 5%.

26:24.165 --> 26:26.293
- There's zero chance.
- Quiet!

26:27.794 --> 26:30.672
And we might all die in the next game.

26:56.197 --> 27:03.204
"GAME" ARENA THIS WAY

27:17.260 --> 27:20.388
Man, this is creepy.

27:39.741 --> 27:41.826
There are other participants?

27:44.996 --> 27:47.374
The game is Zombie Hunt.

27:49.668 --> 27:50.669
Zombies?

27:52.003 --> 27:53.046
Here are the rules.

27:54.172 --> 27:59.135
Each of you will be dealt seven cards.

28:00.011 --> 28:03.598
Use your cards to play one-on-one games

28:03.682 --> 28:08.353
at the special tables
throughout the facility.

28:15.402 --> 28:19.906
Play cards of the same suit
from your hand.

28:21.783 --> 28:25.203
The player with the higher hand wins.

28:25.870 --> 28:30.458
The winner takes one card from the loser.

28:34.921 --> 28:36.715
The higher hand wins.

28:37.799 --> 28:39.050
Easy-peasy.

28:39.718 --> 28:41.720
Where do the zombies come in?

28:42.637 --> 28:46.474
This game has
three kinds of special cards.

28:47.142 --> 28:48.685
The first is…

28:50.687 --> 28:51.813
Zombie cards.

28:52.480 --> 28:54.399
Now I see.

28:56.985 --> 29:01.072
Only one person per team
will be dealt a Zombie card.

29:05.285 --> 29:10.915
The Zombie beats all other cards,
no matter how high they are.

29:11.541 --> 29:14.836
The loser gets infected…

29:17.005 --> 29:19.632
and a Zombie card is added to their hand.

29:21.509 --> 29:24.637
The card that prevents
zombies from multiplying is

29:26.014 --> 29:27.307
the Shotgun card.

29:28.224 --> 29:31.686
You can kill a zombie with this card.

29:33.188 --> 29:37.358
Each player will have one Shotgun card.

29:40.153 --> 29:44.783
You can use it to kill a zombie even if
their Zombie card isn't on the table.

29:45.366 --> 29:48.244
So zombies risk getting killed.

29:48.328 --> 29:51.706
The Shotgun card disappears after one use.

29:51.790 --> 29:54.250
It has no effect on humans.

29:55.627 --> 30:00.173
For those who want a peaceful resolution,
there's the Vaccine card.

30:01.257 --> 30:05.637
Vaccine cards will be
randomly distributed.

30:06.679 --> 30:12.310
Playing the Vaccine card
nullifies a Zombie card on the table…

30:14.854 --> 30:17.565
and turns the zombie back into a human.

30:19.526 --> 30:23.696
However, you cannot use
the Vaccine card on yourself.

30:25.532 --> 30:30.078
Use these two cards
to prevent zombies from multiplying.

30:31.496 --> 30:34.707
The game ends after 20 rounds.

30:35.208 --> 30:40.171
If you run out of number cards
during the 20 rounds,

30:40.255 --> 30:41.506
it's game over.

30:43.132 --> 30:47.804
Whichever side, zombies or humans,
has more members at the end wins.

30:48.304 --> 30:50.557
LARGER SIDE AFTER 20 ROUNDS WINS
HUMANS / ZOMBIES

30:50.640 --> 30:53.393
It's game over
for the side with fewer members.

30:55.061 --> 31:01.901
Each team will enter the game
via one of the four entrances.

31:03.403 --> 31:05.280
There are other teams?

31:06.739 --> 31:10.994
There is also one zombie
on each of the other teams.

31:11.077 --> 31:12.620
So just four?

31:15.665 --> 31:17.709
Game start.

31:18.293 --> 31:20.712
Please take your cards.

31:38.187 --> 31:39.772
No Zombie, please.

31:42.525 --> 31:44.736
First round. Begin.

31:45.737 --> 31:48.615
Please choose an opponent
by touching them,

31:48.698 --> 31:50.867
and then head to a game table.

32:16.059 --> 32:17.936
Please place your cards.

32:20.271 --> 32:23.024
The numbers on the cards
aren't that important.

32:23.942 --> 32:28.237
After 20 rounds, all we need is
to have at least one number card.

32:28.321 --> 32:29.322
Open.

32:32.075 --> 32:33.034
My bad.

32:34.118 --> 32:35.286
Shit.

32:35.370 --> 32:38.247
We might want to avoid
playing other teams.

32:38.331 --> 32:42.085
Why not just play among ourselves
and share number cards?

32:43.544 --> 32:44.587
You're right.

32:45.338 --> 32:47.382
Second round. Begin.

32:47.924 --> 32:52.679
The special cards are a problem,
especially the Zombie card.

32:54.430 --> 32:55.515
Open.

32:57.266 --> 32:58.434
I win.

32:58.518 --> 33:00.269
- Sorry.
- It's okay.

33:01.646 --> 33:02.981
Kinda cramped here.

33:03.481 --> 33:05.692
There are game tables in the basement.

33:06.484 --> 33:10.154
- Let's set up base there.
- Yeah, looks roomy.

33:15.994 --> 33:20.123
The humans win if the zombies are
prevented from multiplying for 20 turns.

33:23.793 --> 33:26.462
There's a zombie on our team, right?

33:28.089 --> 33:31.634
Whoever it is probably won't tell anyone.

33:32.260 --> 33:33.136
Why not?

33:33.219 --> 33:37.473
Because if they're exposed,
they might get killed by a Shotgun card.

33:37.974 --> 33:38.975
Right.

33:40.018 --> 33:42.311
Third round. Begin.

33:43.688 --> 33:44.605
Another team!

33:47.650 --> 33:49.193
- Touch them!
- Okay.

33:51.029 --> 33:51.988
Hey there.

33:54.907 --> 33:55.908
Open.

33:56.951 --> 33:59.037
To keep zombies from multiplying,

33:59.120 --> 34:03.249
we need to find the players
who were randomly dealt Vaccine cards.

34:03.833 --> 34:06.878
That will be our key to victory.

34:06.961 --> 34:07.879
I win.

34:08.379 --> 34:12.341
There doesn't seem to be
a Vaccine card on our team.

34:13.801 --> 34:18.389
That means there's a good chance
a player on another team has one.

34:46.417 --> 34:47.418
Usagi.

35:01.432 --> 35:05.394
Please choose an opponent
by touching them.

35:10.066 --> 35:11.275
Can I ask you something?

35:12.026 --> 35:12.860
What?

35:14.403 --> 35:16.614
I'm looking for a woman named Usagi.

35:17.615 --> 35:18.908
Have you seen her?

35:20.409 --> 35:24.205
She has hair about this long
and is about 160 centimeters tall.

35:24.288 --> 35:27.333
There were tons of women like that.

35:29.544 --> 35:30.545
I see.

35:33.339 --> 35:34.882
But check this out.

35:36.384 --> 35:39.220
This Joker stage seems to be a tournament.

35:40.513 --> 35:44.433
Even if you find her,
you might have to kill each other.

35:48.646 --> 35:50.189
A tournament?

35:50.690 --> 35:55.069
We can't choose the games we play,
and once we get to an arena,

35:56.320 --> 35:59.407
we meet up with players
who survived other arenas.

36:01.159 --> 36:02.743
I think he's right.

36:03.369 --> 36:06.622
It's way different
from when I first came here.

36:07.415 --> 36:09.709
We could choose which games to play.

36:10.334 --> 36:11.460
That's right.

36:11.544 --> 36:16.674
There will only be a few players left
by the end of the tournament.

36:18.676 --> 36:20.469
Those who survive will likely…

36:22.221 --> 36:24.307
Have to kill each other.

36:27.101 --> 36:28.436
Whoa.

36:36.611 --> 36:40.823
Please choose an opponent
by touching them.

36:50.082 --> 36:52.251
Please place your cards.

36:53.419 --> 36:56.964
You've… been infected
by a zombie, haven't you?

36:58.341 --> 36:59.300
What?

36:59.800 --> 37:03.387
You haven't looked me in the eye
since you sat down.

37:04.472 --> 37:08.726
If you wanted to work together and share
number cards, you'd make eye contact.

37:09.227 --> 37:10.478
Well…

37:10.561 --> 37:12.688
On top of that,

37:13.314 --> 37:16.609
you've been playing against the same girl
this whole time.

37:17.443 --> 37:19.987
But you suddenly chose me for this round.

37:20.821 --> 37:25.368
So I figured you turned her
into a zombie and then split up.

37:26.869 --> 37:30.414
Zombies only win
if they infect enough players.

37:41.801 --> 37:44.303
Making more zombies here
isn't a good idea.

37:45.012 --> 37:46.264
Zombies get shot.

37:47.181 --> 37:49.684
But there's no such risk if you're human.

37:51.394 --> 37:54.105
Everyone on this team
still has a Shotgun card.

37:54.897 --> 37:58.025
Someone might kill you
the moment you're exposed.

37:59.735 --> 38:00.611
Listen.

38:01.237 --> 38:04.073
We'll cure you
once we find a Vaccine card.

38:04.949 --> 38:06.784
Stay with us for now.

38:22.258 --> 38:23.259
Open.

39:02.214 --> 39:04.425
Zombies might already be multiplying.

39:06.135 --> 39:07.094
They're zombies?

39:08.054 --> 39:09.889
What should we do with them?

39:11.098 --> 39:13.142
We need to find Vaccine cards.

39:14.101 --> 39:15.227
Hey.

39:16.354 --> 39:19.690
Don't overthink it.
We should just kill them.

39:19.774 --> 39:22.401
We can't simply shoot them.

39:22.485 --> 39:24.779
We have to prevent zombification.

39:24.862 --> 39:26.364
Any ideas?

39:28.449 --> 39:30.284
There is one way.

39:30.951 --> 39:33.496
A way to defend against Zombie cards

39:33.579 --> 39:36.415
without killing each other.

39:42.797 --> 39:45.007
- What is it?
- Careful.

39:45.508 --> 39:47.426
She's not from our team.

39:48.344 --> 39:50.054
She might be a zombie.

39:55.643 --> 40:01.482
We form a group that promises to use
the Vaccine card to cure each other.

40:02.733 --> 40:06.737
Even if one of our members
turns into a zombie,

40:07.238 --> 40:09.782
we'll make sure to cure them.

40:10.825 --> 40:16.414
Then we'll have them tell us
who infected them

40:16.497 --> 40:19.333
and threaten to shoot whoever that is.

40:20.084 --> 40:24.839
That will scare other zombies
away from our group.

40:25.423 --> 40:28.384
A pact to use Vaccine cards
to cure each other?

40:29.301 --> 40:30.511
Will it last?

40:32.721 --> 40:33.973
Let's say…

40:35.891 --> 40:37.685
you're a zombie.

40:37.768 --> 40:38.644
Here.

40:40.187 --> 40:43.774
And say you also have a Vaccine card.

40:46.444 --> 40:50.114
Then suppose you reveal
that you're a zombie

40:50.197 --> 40:55.161
and say you'll promise to use
your Vaccine card on him

40:55.244 --> 40:57.037
if he becomes a zombie.

40:58.205 --> 41:00.374
See what I'm getting at?

41:02.460 --> 41:03.377
What?

41:04.962 --> 41:08.799
You've confessed to being a zombie.

41:09.341 --> 41:12.219
It's like saying, "Kill me anytime."

41:12.803 --> 41:16.724
You mean forming an alliance
by using yourself as a hostage?

41:16.807 --> 41:17.641
Exactly.

41:18.142 --> 41:21.687
You'll keep your promise
because you don't want to die.

41:22.188 --> 41:25.191
You're saying,
"You can kill me if I don't keep it."

41:25.691 --> 41:29.904
The zombie willingly becomes
a hostage for the humans.

41:32.490 --> 41:36.243
And this promise is made
with multiple people.

41:36.744 --> 41:39.371
We create a trust-based group.

41:40.080 --> 41:46.003
We promise to use this vaccine
to cure anyone who turns into a zombie.

41:46.504 --> 41:48.672
But there's only one Vaccine card.

41:48.756 --> 41:52.134
We have to persuade
other Vaccine cardholders to join us.

41:52.218 --> 41:53.719
Are there enough to go around?

41:55.471 --> 41:59.725
None of us know
the total number of Vaccine cards.

42:00.601 --> 42:05.314
We just have to trick
all the other players into believing

42:05.397 --> 42:08.275
that we have enough to save everyone.

42:10.194 --> 42:13.948
Do that, and zombies won't come near us,

42:14.031 --> 42:17.910
and we can win the game
by increasing our numbers.

42:20.037 --> 42:24.792
Okay, but is there really anyone
with both a Zombie and a Vaccine card?

42:25.626 --> 42:27.586
That would be me.

42:28.337 --> 42:29.338
Huh?

42:30.548 --> 42:33.050
That's why you approached us?

42:33.133 --> 42:35.427
Yeah, to make my sales pitch.

42:37.846 --> 42:39.139
What's your name?

42:42.309 --> 42:43.310
Rei.

42:45.354 --> 42:47.064
We'll share the Vaccine card…

42:47.147 --> 42:49.567
This "barricade of trust" strategy

42:49.650 --> 42:53.028
must first be communicated
to the other teams.

42:53.112 --> 42:55.739
Zombies will be too scared
to come near us.

42:56.490 --> 42:59.785
Because if they use
their Zombie card on us,

42:59.868 --> 43:03.497
they will be exposed
and risk getting shot.

43:04.873 --> 43:09.378
We can win if we grow our numbers
with this barricade strategy.

43:11.338 --> 43:12.256
Okay.

43:14.216 --> 43:15.301
Count me in.

43:16.427 --> 43:21.265
There's a group in the basement promising
to use Vaccine cards on each other.

43:21.765 --> 43:25.185
Even if you use a Zombie card,
the Vaccine card will cure them.

43:25.269 --> 43:26.770
That group is trouble.

43:27.271 --> 43:30.441
They keep each other updated
on zombies who came to infect them.

43:30.524 --> 43:33.277
So if you zombify one of them,

43:33.360 --> 43:36.071
they'll tell the others,
and you'll get killed.

43:36.155 --> 43:37.865
Don't tell anyone else,

43:37.948 --> 43:42.036
but I heard a zombie
tried to turn someone from that group,

43:42.536 --> 43:46.790
got exposed, and ended up being killed.

43:47.333 --> 43:48.292
For real?

43:48.375 --> 43:53.088
That group promised to cure each other
with Vaccine cards if they're zombified.

43:53.172 --> 43:57.051
It might be safer to join them
at this point.

43:57.134 --> 43:58.135
They're bad news.

43:58.719 --> 44:01.388
Will this barricade of trust really work?

44:01.889 --> 44:03.349
You'll see.

44:05.934 --> 44:08.520
We'll gather in the basement
and work it out there.

44:09.021 --> 44:10.564
Okay, Miyano.

44:11.065 --> 44:13.192
I have a Vaccine card.

44:13.275 --> 44:14.985
That makes you the third one.

44:15.569 --> 44:16.570
Next.

44:16.654 --> 44:21.367
We'll try to play games among our group,
sharing number cards as we go.

44:22.034 --> 44:25.704
In short, we'll lose on purpose
to those with fewer cards.

44:25.788 --> 44:29.750
And the winner will take
a lower-number card from the loser.

44:32.419 --> 44:35.589
And zombies will only play each other.

44:36.465 --> 44:40.260
That way, we won't have to
kill each other to stop the spread.

44:40.886 --> 44:43.097
And no one runs out of number cards.

44:44.306 --> 44:48.268
We'll get more players who have
Vaccine cards if we keep this up.

45:05.911 --> 45:07.579
It's already the 11th round.

45:07.663 --> 45:10.541
Maybe we should join that basement group.

45:11.041 --> 45:12.960
I heard they gathered Vaccine cards.

45:13.043 --> 45:14.753
Who knows if it's true?

45:24.888 --> 45:28.142
We won't get any more Vaccine cards.

45:28.225 --> 45:31.186
We don't even know how many there are.

45:32.646 --> 45:35.357
Simply threatening zombies isn't enough.

45:35.441 --> 45:38.318
There's a way to increase
our odds of survival.

45:39.820 --> 45:40.696
How?

45:43.365 --> 45:45.534
Reduce the number of zombies.

45:51.373 --> 45:52.833
I get it.

45:54.543 --> 45:56.378
This dude turned into a zombie.

45:58.380 --> 45:59.381
Put him in there.

46:11.977 --> 46:15.147
Do you remember who turned you?

46:17.107 --> 46:18.108
Yeah.

46:23.530 --> 46:24.406
We'll kill 'em.

46:33.165 --> 46:34.166
Hey,

46:35.918 --> 46:37.753
would you do it?

46:40.756 --> 46:43.050
We'll guarantee you vaccine priority.

46:59.107 --> 47:01.068
Please place your cards.

47:21.588 --> 47:22.548
Open.

47:42.401 --> 47:45.070
You said you wanted out too!

47:45.863 --> 47:48.949
Are you gonna shoot me, a blood brother?!

47:49.032 --> 47:50.075
No, stop!

48:11.680 --> 48:14.099
Kazuya, you…

48:18.478 --> 48:19.646
It had to be done.

48:22.441 --> 48:23.734
This is a game.

48:38.749 --> 48:40.167
Nice work!

48:41.418 --> 48:43.921
You're not some law-abiding chump.

48:45.797 --> 48:47.174
Take note, everyone.

48:48.634 --> 48:51.970
Everyone who was zombified
has info on the other zombies.

48:53.263 --> 48:55.515
Get info from the other teams too.

48:56.141 --> 48:57.225
How?

49:00.812 --> 49:02.898
Threaten them with a Shotgun card.

49:03.649 --> 49:05.025
They'll talk.

49:08.195 --> 49:11.573
I like your style. Let's keep it up, eh?

49:49.444 --> 49:54.074
Tell me who the zombies are,
and we'll give you vaccine priority.

49:54.825 --> 49:58.078
Okay! I'll tell you the ones I know!

50:04.793 --> 50:07.379
We're dead if they find out we're zombies.

50:08.046 --> 50:09.381
We have to hide.

50:10.007 --> 50:10.882
Listen.

50:11.758 --> 50:14.052
We'll trap them and turn them.

50:15.053 --> 50:16.847
At this point, anyone will do!

50:18.932 --> 50:20.392
- Come on.
- Right.

50:26.773 --> 50:27.649
Open.

50:44.958 --> 50:46.460
This is not good.

50:46.960 --> 50:48.336
Yeah.

50:48.962 --> 50:49.963
Don't you care?

50:51.465 --> 50:55.218
The barricade of trust is holding up.

50:57.012 --> 50:59.973
The zombies on the other teams
will retaliate.

51:05.520 --> 51:08.607
It's starting to feel like a real game.

53:39.299 --> 53:42.260
Subtitle translation by: Jason Franzman
